{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/12779","id":5446125367,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRJ1HNw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12779","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12779.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/12779.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/12779","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/12779/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/12779/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/12779/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/7ef595a2d54926c4cab0b320ab9fda2f918fb4d7","number":12779,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fleet gh close guard + closed-bound detective (#9177 controls 1+2)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements the two remaining controls from #9177 (the 2026-11-13 Fleet CA incident on #9155). Control 3 (App-write attribution) already landed in #12076, which stays canonical.\n\n## Fix 1 — preventive close guard in `fleet gh`\n\n`issue close` and `issue edit --add-label status:done` are refused (exit 2, before token rotation) when the queue broker holds a live bound task for that repo#issue — `claimed` or `parked` **and** carrying a non-empty `claim_session_id` — unless the caller presents the bound task's completion record with the wrapper-only `--completion-record <path>` flag (stripped before gh runs). The record must be a `fleet-closure/v1` object with `action: \"close\"`, matching `item.number` and `binding.task_id`. Issues without a live bound task are unaffected.\n\n- New `crates/fleet/src/gh_guard.rs`, wired into `gh.rs` `run()` ahead of the closure parse.\n- Broker lookup via new library-shaped `fleet_queue::client::guard_rows(limit)` (paged rich /list over claimed+parked, never prints/exits).\n- Rich /list select now includes `claim_session_id` (`turso_queue/admin.rs`).\n- Broker unreachable → **fail-open** with a stderr note (an outage must not block every close; the detective is the net). Build without the queue client skips the guard.\n\n## Fix 2 — detective control on the sweep\n\nNew `turso_queue/closed_bound.rs`: every sweep cycle now runs a closed-bound pass — each session-stamped claimed|parked task's issue is read on GitHub once per pass (per-pass cache) and crossed with the closure log (`FLEET_CLOSURE_LOG`, else the state dir's `closure-records.jsonl`). A landed issue with no completion record for its bound task appends a `closed_bound_alert` event and POSTs one warning-severity throat alert (`closed-bound:<task_id>` key, source `fleet-queue`).\n\n- Same \"bound\" definition as the guard, so the two controls agree.\n- Fail-open: no probe, unreadable GitHub (Unknown) or unreadable log never alerts; post failures are counted in the summary, never fatal; a detective error never fails the sweep.\n- Opt out with `closed_bound=false`; `closed_bound_limit` (default 200); summary in `out[\"closed_bound\"]`; a cycle with `missing_record > 0` lands in the sweep event.\n- `needs_drew.rs` gains a small `post_plain_alert_to` transport helper (same transport/error contract as the needs-drew raise).\n\n## Verification\n\nLocal targeted run (per CI policy — no PR checks, nightly main CI):\n\n```\ncargo test --manifest-path pkgs/fleet/Cargo.toml -p fleet -p fleet-queue --locked\n# fleet: 95 passed (incl. 3 gh_guard tests)\n# fleet-queue: 522 passed (incl. 8 closed_bound tests)\n# integration bins: 16 passed — 0 failures\n```\n\nTest oracles: bound+no-record refused / bound+record allowed / unbound unaffected / status:done treated as close (guard); closed-without-record alerts / closed-with-record quiet / fail-open on probe-or-post failure (detective); the fleet-closure/v1 contract as merged in #11440.\n\nRefs #9177. Not marked `Closes #9177`: the issue's third acceptance item (attribution) landed separately in #12076; close will be evaluated against the issue's done check once this merges.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/run-proof?expires=1797993474&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=12779&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F12779&variant=proof_this_pr&signature=4ea8f0dc51f06c7ad21e634984a8c2b18175ecd914348297db9449507a9425f9\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Proof this PR\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-dark-3x.png\" width=\"121\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/12779?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-23T02:37:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-27T10:51:55Z","closed_at":"2026-11-23T02:38:52Z","merged_at":"2026-11-23T02:38:52Z","merge_commit_sha":"dc5ed627b5e2f56a5c87cc8b20930bdf533888d6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/20352-9177-close-guard-detective","ref":"queue/20352-9177-close-guard-detective","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-tod